    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Explanation of how the organization has determined which sites and which products and services in its supply chain have the most significant actual and potential impacts on biodiversity</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Explain how the organization has determined which of its sites and which products and services in its supply chain have the most significant actual and potential impacts on biodiversity. Sites include those owned, leased, or managed by the organization, including subsurface infrastructures and announced or no-longer-active sites. Supply chain coverage extends to suppliers beyond the first tier; downstream value-chain entities may also be reported.</skos:definition>
    <sds:hasUnit rdf:resource="Text"/>
    <sds:hasTemporalGranularity rdf:resource="https://sustainabilitydataspace.com/ontology#Annual"/>
  </rdf:Description>
