    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Describe remuneration policies for termination payments. Termination payments include all payments and benefits given to a departing member of the highest governance body or senior executive whose appointment is terminated, extending beyond monetary payments to transferring property or automatic/accelerated vesting of incentives. If termination payments are provided, explain whether notice periods, termination payments, additional non-notice payments, and any mitigation clauses differ between highest governance body members/senior executives and other employees.</skos:definition>
